WEBVTT


00:01:32.200 --> 00:01:35.100
I know it's further away but
you'll see your mates at school.


00:01:36.000 --> 00:01:38.200
And we'll have the new
baby for company soon.


00:01:38.300 --> 00:01:39.300
I liked it here.


00:02:14.600 --> 00:02:15.600
Ta-da!


00:02:20.600 --> 00:02:21.600
What do you think?


00:02:24.400 --> 00:02:26.365
Say something, then.


00:02:26.400 --> 00:02:28.400
It looks like it's
about to fall down.


00:02:29.500 --> 00:02:33.200
Nothing's about to
fall down. Trust me.


00:02:45.800 --> 00:02:47.300
This'll be useful.


00:02:49.500 --> 00:02:51.050
In 50 years' time.


00:02:51.085 --> 00:02:52.600
Come through here.


00:02:57.300 --> 00:02:59.600
You've got to picture it
in your mind's eye, son.


00:02:59.635 --> 00:03:02.100
- Your what?
- Your mind's eye.


00:03:02.200 --> 00:03:04.200
Your imagination. Here.


00:03:05.600 --> 00:03:07.300
No, it's still a dump.


00:03:11.200 --> 00:03:15.600
Mikey... you know the flat wasn't
big enough for the three of us,


00:03:15.635 --> 00:03:17.200
especially with the baby.


00:04:33.500 --> 00:04:35.000
We did it, hey?


00:04:36.000 --> 00:04:38.600
There's just so much to do.


00:04:38.700 --> 00:04:41.300
I know it doesn't look much
but I'll get it all done up.


00:04:41.335 --> 00:04:43.200
I know you will.


00:04:48.600 --> 00:04:50.500
How come the toilet's
not in the toilet?


00:04:50.600 --> 00:04:55.700
Er... the man who lived
here was... well, he was old


00:04:55.800 --> 00:04:57.865
and he couldn't move easily.


00:04:57.900 --> 00:05:00.500
- What happened to him?
- He died here.


00:05:00.600 --> 00:05:03.700
- What, in this room?
- On the toilet.


00:05:03.735 --> 00:05:06.865
- Dave!
- Joking! I'm joking!


00:05:06.900 --> 00:05:09.500
Mr Myers passed away in
the vicinity of the kitchen,


00:05:09.535 --> 00:05:11.767
whilst partaking of
a bottle of fine ale!


00:05:11.802 --> 00:05:14.001
But it was a week
before they found him.


00:05:14.036 --> 00:05:16.200
The smell drifted
down the whole street.


00:05:17.100 --> 00:05:20.800
It was like old
socks and rotten fish.


00:05:21.700 --> 00:05:23.700
Is that a smile?


00:05:23.800 --> 00:05:27.400
Bugger me, it is! A sm... Lou...
Look at that! It's a smile!


00:05:30.300 --> 00:05:31.800
Watch the plant, please!


00:05:32.800 --> 00:05:34.200
I want the room
by the bathroom.


00:05:37.000 --> 00:05:38.600
I need that room for
the baby, my love.


00:05:41.000 --> 00:05:44.200
We thought you'd like the top
room. You know, a bit of privacy.


00:05:47.100 --> 00:05:48.500
Michael...


00:06:00.700 --> 00:06:02.850
Hey, careful. You'll
fall right through.


00:06:02.885 --> 00:06:05.000
A couple of those
boards need replacing.


00:06:05.800 --> 00:06:09.100
Give us a hand downstairs.
Some boxes need shifting.


00:06:09.200 --> 00:06:10.565
But I've moved all my things.


00:06:10.600 --> 00:06:13.200
Michael, I don't want your
mum carrying stuff, OK?


00:06:16.000 --> 00:06:17.400
Hello, Cooper Cabs.


00:06:19.100 --> 00:06:20.600
Get down there now.


00:06:21.900 --> 00:06:24.400
Yeah, no problem.
Where are you?


00:07:35.300 --> 00:07:38.400
- Mum, there's spiders all over my room.
- They're harmless, my love.


00:07:40.300 --> 00:07:43.200
Maybe you could skip school
today. Stay and give us a hand.


00:07:43.235 --> 00:07:45.100
- Are you serious?
- Yeah.


00:07:45.135 --> 00:07:46.500
Just me and you.


00:07:46.600 --> 00:07:49.100
- Is Dad working?
- Get more done without him.


00:07:50.100 --> 00:07:53.300
You can help me pick out
colours for the baby's room.


00:07:53.400 --> 00:07:55.800
Maybe we should have found
out what we're having.


00:07:55.900 --> 00:07:57.700
It'd make decorating
a bit easier.


00:07:59.000 --> 00:08:00.065
What?


00:08:00.100 --> 00:08:03.065
Nothing. Just remembered
I've got a test.


00:08:03.100 --> 00:08:05.800
Well, I can phone your school
and let them know that I need you.


00:08:07.400 --> 00:08:08.400
See you, then.


00:08:10.400 --> 00:08:15.365
# And through it all
she offers me protection


00:08:15.400 --> 00:08:21.400
# A lot of love and affection
whether I'm right or wrong


00:08:21.500 --> 00:08:27.200
# And down the waterfall
wherever it may take me


00:08:27.300 --> 00:08:33.700
# I know that life won't
break me when I come to call


00:08:33.735 --> 00:08:36.500
# She won't forsake me


00:08:38.600 --> 00:08:41.100
# I'm loving angels instead #


00:08:52.500 --> 00:08:55.700
And that, lads,
is how it's done.


00:08:56.700 --> 00:08:57.965
Very impressive, Mr Leakey.


00:08:58.000 --> 00:09:00.700
Glad we've finally found
one subject you could master.


00:09:02.000 --> 00:09:04.200
Right, who's next?


00:09:07.800 --> 00:09:10.100
Michael Cooper.


00:09:15.600 --> 00:09:18.965
It's easy. You can do it.


00:09:19.000 --> 00:09:21.200
He doesn't like
being so high up, sir.


00:09:21.235 --> 00:09:23.617
Oh, that's right,
yes. Sorry, I forgot.


00:09:23.652 --> 00:09:26.000
- He's got a phobia.
- Come on, Mikey!


00:09:34.300 --> 00:09:37.500
- Well?
- It makes me feel sick, sir.


00:09:37.535 --> 00:09:38.900
Mikey, you can do it, man!


00:09:40.600 --> 00:09:43.265
All right, get back
down here. 20 lengths.


00:09:43.300 --> 00:09:45.700
Right, which one of you is
gonna show me some guts, then?


00:09:46.700 --> 00:09:49.200
Well, don't put your hands
up all at once, will you?


00:09:50.800 --> 00:09:53.265
"It makes me feel sick, sir. "


00:09:53.300 --> 00:09:55.850
It makes me feel sick
and all and I gotta do it.


00:09:55.885 --> 00:09:58.400
- Give it a rest, Coot.
- And I got a dodgy ear.


00:09:58.500 --> 00:10:01.300
- You got dodgy hair to match!
- At least I'm not a wuss!


00:10:01.400 --> 00:10:03.600
Maybe he don't wanna
belly-flop like you, Coot.


00:10:10.900 --> 00:10:12.300
Want a lift?


00:10:13.400 --> 00:10:15.400
It's OK, Dad's not
on for another hour.


00:10:15.435 --> 00:10:17.400
Nah, I'll hang
around here for a bit.


00:10:18.700 --> 00:10:20.365
Things bad at home?


00:10:20.400 --> 00:10:23.700
Stepdad's back. Till
she kicks him out again!


00:10:24.800 --> 00:10:27.800
Hey! I'll start the
meter in a minute.


00:10:27.835 --> 00:10:29.800
You'll be all
right, won't you?


00:10:43.200 --> 00:10:45.100
Hi, Dad.


00:10:49.700 --> 00:10:51.100
# Sha-la-boom-boom,
yeah


00:10:51.200 --> 00:10:53.500
# Do it, do it, do it, do it


00:10:53.600 --> 00:10:56.400
# Sha-la-boom-boom,
yeah


00:11:16.700 --> 00:11:18.450
# Sha-la-boom-boom,
yeah


00:11:18.485 --> 00:11:20.200
# Ooh, do it easy...


00:11:27.900 --> 00:11:30.400
# Sha-la-boom-boom,
yeah #


00:12:07.400 --> 00:12:09.900
# Oh, take me higher... #


00:12:10.000 --> 00:12:11.300
Oh, no. Please,
please, please.


00:12:27.800 --> 00:12:29.400
Who's there?


00:12:38.800 --> 00:12:40.200
Mum!


00:12:42.900 --> 00:12:44.700
Mum, what shall I do?


00:13:21.400 --> 00:13:22.400
Dad.


00:13:27.000 --> 00:13:30.300
- You've got a baby sister.
- A sister?


00:13:36.600 --> 00:13:38.200
Thank God you were there.


00:13:55.000 --> 00:13:56.600
Caught us by
surprise, didn't she?


00:14:02.500 --> 00:14:05.300
- Can she come home?
- Soon, we hope.


00:14:08.000 --> 00:14:10.600
The doctors say
she's a real fighter.


00:14:18.000 --> 00:14:21.100
Did you see that? She
looked right at me.


00:14:41.500 --> 00:14:43.300
Mikey.


00:14:43.400 --> 00:14:45.800
I just had a look in
that shed down the bottom,


00:14:45.835 --> 00:14:47.465
full of worthless old junk.


00:14:47.500 --> 00:14:49.565
You didn't? There
wasn't anything else?


00:14:49.600 --> 00:14:52.200
You stay away from it. Do you
hear? It's a bloody death trap.


00:14:53.500 --> 00:14:56.500
- I better get started in here.
- I can... help if you want.


00:14:58.300 --> 00:15:00.100
Are you feeling all right?


00:15:00.135 --> 00:15:01.700
Come on, then.


00:15:06.800 --> 00:15:09.200
Right, you start
clearing all this up.


00:15:10.800 --> 00:15:14.100
# If the fish swam
out of the ocean


00:15:14.200 --> 00:15:17.800
# And grew legs and
they started walking


00:15:17.835 --> 00:15:21.017
# And the apes climbed
down from the trees


00:15:21.052 --> 00:15:24.200
# And grew tall and
they started talking...


00:15:24.300 --> 00:15:26.365
Original tiles.


00:15:26.400 --> 00:15:28.400
# And the stars
fell out of the sky


00:15:28.500 --> 00:15:31.700
# And my tears
rolled into the ocean


00:15:31.735 --> 00:15:34.900
# Now I'm looking
for a reason why... #


00:15:42.000 --> 00:15:43.465
- Dad?
- Uh-huh?


00:15:43.500 --> 00:15:46.000
Do you think Mum would
have had the baby yesterday


00:15:46.100 --> 00:15:47.400
if we hadn't moved house?


00:15:48.800 --> 00:15:49.900
I don't know, Mikey.


00:15:53.300 --> 00:15:55.065
Do you think if I'd
given her more of a hand


00:15:55.100 --> 00:15:57.600
and stayed home from school
she would have been all right?


00:16:00.800 --> 00:16:02.500
Here.


00:16:02.535 --> 00:16:04.200
Take it.


00:16:06.300 --> 00:16:07.400
Go on.


00:16:12.200 --> 00:16:14.565
Go on! That's it.


00:16:14.600 --> 00:16:17.000
Smash it up. Get it
all out of your system.


00:16:19.300 --> 00:16:21.065
You know your problem, Mikey?


00:16:21.100 --> 00:16:24.000
You think too much.
Sometimes you've just gotta...


00:16:24.100 --> 00:16:25.100
let go.


00:16:26.800 --> 00:16:31.200
That's it. Carry on like that,
I'll let you have a go on that shed.


00:16:57.300 --> 00:16:58.700
You're the new boy.


00:16:58.800 --> 00:17:00.100
I'm Mina.


00:17:00.200 --> 00:17:01.900
Yeah?


00:17:02.000 --> 00:17:04.600
I'm Mina and you are?


00:17:05.700 --> 00:17:06.965
Michael.


00:17:07.000 --> 00:17:09.800
I live just across
those fields.


00:17:11.800 --> 00:17:14.200
And you're the closest thing
I've got to a neighbour.


00:17:14.235 --> 00:17:15.900
Well, a human one.


00:17:17.500 --> 00:17:19.900
I suppose you'll be
putting down lawn.


00:17:19.935 --> 00:17:21.500
Typical!


00:17:21.600 --> 00:17:24.000
Your garden's home to a
multitude of creatures.


00:17:24.035 --> 00:17:26.400
You know that's our
wall you're sitting on?


00:17:29.600 --> 00:17:30.800
Your wall, is it?


00:18:16.300 --> 00:18:18.800
Here.


00:18:24.000 --> 00:18:25.500
Who are you?


00:18:31.600 --> 00:18:32.700
Go away.


00:18:37.700 --> 00:18:39.600
Scram!


00:18:41.400 --> 00:18:43.400
They're just being
cautious, love.


00:18:43.500 --> 00:18:45.800
They've got to play
it safe, haven't they?


00:18:46.600 --> 00:18:48.300
Please, Lou, don't cry.


00:18:50.700 --> 00:18:52.500
It's gonna be OK, I promise.


00:18:55.200 --> 00:18:56.600
It'll be OK.


00:18:58.400 --> 00:18:59.500
I know.


00:19:02.800 --> 00:19:05.400
I've got you a ticket for the
County Diving Championship.


00:19:05.435 --> 00:19:06.400
Oh, thanks!


00:19:06.500 --> 00:19:08.800
I'm gonna get gold,
man. I know it.


00:19:10.700 --> 00:19:13.600
Look after that, Mikey. You're
the only person I've got coming.


00:19:15.200 --> 00:19:18.600
Leakey, so guess what I
found down the garden shed?


00:19:18.635 --> 00:19:21.000
This guy. Homeless. Must be.


00:19:21.100 --> 00:19:24.400
- I hope you told him to shift it.
- Yeah, course.


00:19:25.300 --> 00:19:28.300
He was weird, though.
He looked really sick.


00:19:28.335 --> 00:19:31.300
Mikey, don't be thick!
The guy's a junkie!


00:19:31.400 --> 00:19:34.900
You'll probably never see him
again. Come on, before we're late.


00:19:54.100 --> 00:19:59.100
Evolution. Do you see how the head
changes shape to hold our big brains?


00:20:02.500 --> 00:20:06.600
Did I say, "big brains"? Maybe
I should qualify that, Mr Coot.


00:20:06.700 --> 00:20:10.200
Right, get out your
exercise books, everyone.


00:20:12.500 --> 00:20:13.900
What?!


00:20:16.200 --> 00:20:17.800
Quiet!


00:20:18.900 --> 00:20:21.900
- Michael, where did these come from?
- I don't know, sir!


00:20:22.000 --> 00:20:23.600
- OK, calm down. Wait.
- I dunno!


00:20:23.700 --> 00:20:25.500
- Leakey, was this you?
- No, sir!


00:20:25.535 --> 00:20:27.000
Leakey! Don't touch anything!


00:20:28.300 --> 00:20:31.600
Quiet, everyone! Calm down!


00:20:41.900 --> 00:20:44.800
- Do you like birds?
- I suppose.


00:20:44.835 --> 00:20:47.000
Do you like drawing?


00:20:47.100 --> 00:20:49.600
Well, it's better than
history and physics.


00:20:49.700 --> 00:20:51.600
Do you draw the
things around you?


00:20:51.700 --> 00:20:54.000
You ask a lot of
questions, don't you?


00:20:54.100 --> 00:20:56.500
Drawing makes you look
at the world more closely.


00:20:56.535 --> 00:21:00.300
- Helps you notice the details.
- Whatever.


00:21:05.000 --> 00:21:08.400
Didn't anyone ever tell
you it's rude to stare?


00:21:08.500 --> 00:21:10.800
Anyway, I notice plenty.


00:21:10.900 --> 00:21:13.300
Yeah? What colour's
a blackbird?


00:21:15.200 --> 00:21:16.600
Black?


00:21:18.200 --> 00:21:21.000
By the way, there's
an insect in your hair.


00:21:23.600 --> 00:21:25.900
Like I said, details.


00:22:03.200 --> 00:22:07.100
They're slow-moving
little critters, these are.


00:22:08.700 --> 00:22:09.700
Even in the gut.


00:22:35.600 --> 00:22:37.400
We've got lots of
proper food inside.


00:22:38.500 --> 00:22:42.100
We've got crisps, different
flavours, chocolate, fish fingers.


00:22:43.600 --> 00:22:49.600
27... 53.


00:22:50.800 --> 00:22:52.100
What?


00:22:53.400 --> 00:22:55.300
They're pretty,
aren't they, hmm?


00:22:58.000 --> 00:22:59.500
Are you Mr Myers?


00:22:59.600 --> 00:23:01.400
That old git's dead.


00:23:03.300 --> 00:23:05.500
Are you a... Are you a junkie?


00:23:06.500 --> 00:23:08.000
No, I'm not a junkie.


00:23:08.100 --> 00:23:10.000
I'm just junk.


00:23:11.000 --> 00:23:13.000
I'm worthless old junk.


00:23:17.800 --> 00:23:19.400
Let me help you.


00:23:21.300 --> 00:23:22.900
You wanna help me?


00:23:26.600 --> 00:23:29.100
Well, forget I exist.


00:23:29.900 --> 00:23:31.765
Pretend I'm a bad dream.


00:23:31.800 --> 00:23:35.000
Then you'll wake up
and, bingo, I'm gone.


00:23:44.100 --> 00:23:46.400
There's no power.


00:23:53.100 --> 00:23:54.800
Damn you.


00:24:21.700 --> 00:24:25.200
- How are you feeling, Gracie?
- Never better, dear!


00:24:28.700 --> 00:24:33.500
You can't let 'em give up on
you. Then you're really done for.


00:24:33.600 --> 00:24:36.465
I have to keep moving, me.


00:24:36.500 --> 00:24:41.700
I go once up and down the ward and
three times round every landing.


00:24:41.735 --> 00:24:45.100
I do that every day.
It keeps Arthur away.


00:24:45.135 --> 00:24:46.765
Arthur?


00:24:46.800 --> 00:24:49.800
My old friend,
Mr Arthur-itis!


00:24:52.800 --> 00:24:57.000
I'm absolutely knackered, me,


00:24:57.100 --> 00:24:59.600
but I'll be
dancing again soon.


00:25:00.500 --> 00:25:03.700
Have you got a little baby
brother or a sister in here?


00:25:03.735 --> 00:25:05.500
Sister.


00:25:06.200 --> 00:25:08.800
My baby's all grown up now.


00:25:08.900 --> 00:25:12.500
He was a lovely
little boy... like you.


00:25:13.400 --> 00:25:16.900
Busy man now. Very busy man.


00:25:18.300 --> 00:25:20.000
Coming next weekend, he says.


00:25:22.600 --> 00:25:26.900
Here... what is it with
grapes and hospitals?


00:25:27.000 --> 00:25:29.100
I've never had so
many in my life!


00:25:31.000 --> 00:25:32.365
Thanks.


00:25:32.400 --> 00:25:34.600
Well, gotta get moving.


00:25:36.800 --> 00:25:39.300
It keeps the ticker ticking.


00:25:51.400 --> 00:25:54.400
How's your dad's cooking?
Is he doing all right?


00:25:54.500 --> 00:25:56.800
- Too many veggies!
- Yeah?


00:25:58.300 --> 00:25:59.300
Doctor...


00:26:00.600 --> 00:26:03.800
You would tell me if
anything was wrong.


00:26:03.835 --> 00:26:05.800
Course I would, darling.


00:26:46.600 --> 00:26:48.600
You didn't tell me
you had a sister.


00:26:51.300 --> 00:26:53.300
Are you all right? Are you OK?


00:26:53.400 --> 00:26:55.800
What are you doing
creeping up on me like that?


00:26:55.835 --> 00:26:58.200
- You shouldn't feel embarrassed.
- I don't!


00:26:59.700 --> 00:27:03.600
- How is she, your sister?
- She's in hospital.


00:27:04.900 --> 00:27:07.500
- What's her name?
- She hasn't got one yet.


00:27:07.535 --> 00:27:09.500
Mum and Dad haven't had time.


00:27:10.700 --> 00:27:13.300
- Doesn't your school have a uniform?
- I don't go to school.


00:27:14.400 --> 00:27:15.600
My mother educates me.


00:27:15.700 --> 00:27:19.700
That's weird, not going to school.
What about seeing your mates?


00:27:21.500 --> 00:27:25.600
"How can the bird that is born
for joy sit in a cage and sing?"


00:27:26.800 --> 00:27:30.165
- You've heard of William Blake?
- No.


00:27:30.200 --> 00:27:33.600
He wrote poems and painted pictures.
A lot of the time he lived nude.


00:27:33.700 --> 00:27:37.350
You mean, with no clothes on?
With his tackle hanging out?


00:27:37.385 --> 00:27:41.000
He was extraordinary. He
even saw angels in his garden.


00:27:42.500 --> 00:27:44.100
He sounds like a nutter.


00:27:50.900 --> 00:27:52.400
Champions League tonight, son.


00:27:55.000 --> 00:27:56.500
Right, what's on the menu?


00:27:56.535 --> 00:27:58.665
Not pizza again.


00:27:58.700 --> 00:28:01.700
How about Chinese? That'll
have a few veg in it!


00:28:01.735 --> 00:28:04.700
- All right.
- Here you are. What do you fancy?


00:28:14.000 --> 00:28:15.400
27 and 53.


00:28:18.700 --> 00:28:19.900
Blimey, that was quick!


00:28:22.900 --> 00:28:24.200
OK...


00:29:10.800 --> 00:29:13.400
I've got a knife and
fork or chopsticks.


00:29:35.200 --> 00:29:38.800
27, 53. Food of the dogs.


00:29:40.200 --> 00:29:42.000
You're not as
stupid as you look.


00:29:42.035 --> 00:29:44.000
A fortune cookie?


00:29:48.300 --> 00:29:52.100
Fortune?


00:29:59.400 --> 00:30:03.800
You having a good look, are
you? You're nosy, you are.


00:30:04.700 --> 00:30:08.000
- I think you should see a doctor.
- Why?


00:30:10.200 --> 00:30:12.800
Why me? Why now?


00:30:13.800 --> 00:30:14.800
I don't know.


00:30:14.900 --> 00:30:18.100
There must be some other sick
soul you can inflict yourself on.


00:30:19.600 --> 00:30:22.300
No, I can't help them.


00:30:40.800 --> 00:30:42.400
Get off!


00:30:44.800 --> 00:30:46.600
Are you a hunchback?


00:30:50.800 --> 00:30:53.300
Your back, what's on it?


00:30:54.300 --> 00:30:56.000
Nothing. It's
no good any more.


00:31:10.200 --> 00:31:12.400
Of course, he doesn't
look like that now.


00:31:12.435 --> 00:31:13.400
A bit of grey.


00:31:13.500 --> 00:31:16.000
Like me.


00:31:16.100 --> 00:31:19.500
He couldn't make it this time
but next weekend, he says.


00:31:19.600 --> 00:31:21.800
We're taking the
baby home today.


00:31:21.900 --> 00:31:27.565
Oh... to go home,
what a feeling.


00:31:27.600 --> 00:31:31.000
- When are they letting you out?
- Oh, any time now.


00:31:34.000 --> 00:31:38.065
- Grace... do your hands hurt?
- Mm.


00:31:38.100 --> 00:31:41.800
Arthur and me, we're
old friends, we are.


00:31:41.835 --> 00:31:44.667
I know someone
who's got arthritis.


00:31:44.702 --> 00:31:47.251
Tell him from me
to keep moving.


00:31:47.286 --> 00:31:49.800
And cod-liver
oil. That helps.


00:31:52.200 --> 00:31:55.000
He lives in my garden shed.


00:31:55.100 --> 00:31:57.700
There's a lot of
homeless about these days.


00:32:00.200 --> 00:32:04.600
He's not like us.
Not a normal person.


00:32:05.800 --> 00:32:07.200
He's something different.


00:32:07.300 --> 00:32:10.400
Given up on life, has he?


00:32:10.500 --> 00:32:13.500
He doesn't care...
about anything.


00:32:13.600 --> 00:32:16.700
He just sits there,
like he's waiting to die


00:32:16.735 --> 00:32:18.667
and I don't know what to do.


00:32:18.702 --> 00:32:20.600
You mustn't ever give up.


00:32:22.200 --> 00:32:24.400
Here, have a grape.


00:33:19.300 --> 00:33:21.000
Not bad.


00:33:23.200 --> 00:33:25.000
Not bad at all.


00:33:26.100 --> 00:33:28.200
And no toilet.


00:33:28.300 --> 00:33:30.200
It's not gone far, though.


00:33:33.300 --> 00:33:35.550
I thought it'd make
a nice garden scene.


00:33:35.585 --> 00:33:37.800
I thought that shed
was coming down.


00:33:39.400 --> 00:33:41.865
But Dad promised me
some shelves first!


00:33:41.900 --> 00:33:44.800
It's true, I did. He's
living out of a suitcase.


00:33:45.600 --> 00:33:47.000
I'll get round
to it, I promise.


00:33:48.200 --> 00:33:49.800
It's next on my list.


00:34:04.400 --> 00:34:05.900
Did we wake you?


00:34:07.300 --> 00:34:12.700
- Is she gonna be all right, then?
- Yeah, my love. Everything's fine.


00:34:15.200 --> 00:34:17.400
I think you've got taller
these last few days.


00:34:17.500 --> 00:34:20.100
- Believe me.
- Mum...


00:34:20.200 --> 00:34:21.500
Come here.


00:34:23.200 --> 00:34:24.600
Come here a sec.


00:34:33.500 --> 00:34:35.600
You'll always be my
baby, you know that.


00:34:57.000 --> 00:35:01.100
Don't jump too high. Wouldn't want
you getting scared now, would we?


00:35:03.300 --> 00:35:06.400
Right now, you lot, pay
attention. Eyes on me, Lee.


00:35:15.000 --> 00:35:18.600
You're gonna take your shirts
off. You can do it in skins, right?


00:35:18.700 --> 00:35:20.300
Yes, sir.


00:35:20.400 --> 00:35:23.400
Anyone says they're cold, they can
run round the field three times.


00:35:23.435 --> 00:35:28.200
- Have I made myself clear?
- Yes, sir!


00:35:39.500 --> 00:35:41.900
Hey, hey! Don't eat those!


00:35:42.000 --> 00:35:43.800
They could be poisonous.


00:35:45.900 --> 00:35:47.900
I got you these aspirins.


00:35:49.500 --> 00:35:52.000
- A bleeding-good Samaritan,
you are. - Just take 'em.


00:35:52.035 --> 00:35:53.500
They'll make you feel better.


00:36:06.600 --> 00:36:09.265
That is a vile,
unnatural brew, that is!


00:36:09.300 --> 00:36:13.000
You eat flies, beetles and
spiders and you spit this out?


00:36:13.100 --> 00:36:15.265
- You ever tasted spiders' legs?
- No.


00:36:15.300 --> 00:36:18.100
Well, you're hardly in a position
to comment, then, are you?


00:36:24.200 --> 00:36:26.800
It's my sister.
She's not been well.


00:36:29.400 --> 00:36:34.200
Babies... Spew muck,
spittle and tears out.


00:36:34.300 --> 00:36:37.200
It's good she's crying.
It means she's strong.


00:36:40.900 --> 00:36:42.900
How did you know
about 27 and 53?


00:36:45.000 --> 00:36:49.100
You used to hear him on the
phone. Most nights he'd ring 'em.


00:36:49.200 --> 00:36:53.500
What? You mean you left the
shed? Do you do that now ever?


00:36:53.600 --> 00:36:55.200
Never.


00:36:55.300 --> 00:36:57.200
A never-ending never.


00:36:58.000 --> 00:37:01.100
But with Ernie, though, you
used to go inside the house?


00:37:01.200 --> 00:37:03.400
I used to find his
leavings by the bin.


00:37:04.400 --> 00:37:06.800
That and a bottle of brown.


00:37:06.900 --> 00:37:13.100
Brown ale. It's the
sweetest of nectars, that is.


00:37:15.400 --> 00:37:17.700
Did he see you?


00:37:17.800 --> 00:37:20.400
He used to look
right through me.


00:37:22.200 --> 00:37:24.100
Perhaps he thought
I was a figment.


00:37:25.700 --> 00:37:27.200
You think I'm a figment.


00:37:35.900 --> 00:37:37.100
I'm not sure what you are.


00:38:01.600 --> 00:38:03.500
- You're dead!
- Only wounded!


00:38:11.700 --> 00:38:16.000
I found it in my stepdad's things.
I'll put it back after, though.


00:38:16.100 --> 00:38:17.900
He'll never even
notice it's gone.


00:38:21.300 --> 00:38:23.600
Reckon I could hit one?


00:38:23.700 --> 00:38:27.500
I've been practising. I
could kill it stone-dead.


00:38:36.100 --> 00:38:37.965
Leakey!


00:38:38.000 --> 00:38:40.300
What's going on?
Stupid rabbit!


00:38:40.400 --> 00:38:42.800
- I think it's a hare.
- Not any more.


00:38:50.500 --> 00:38:52.900
- Where are you going?
- Something's wrong.


00:39:05.400 --> 00:39:07.500
It's not OK.
Don't tell me that!


00:39:07.600 --> 00:39:11.900
They told me to bring her
in. How is that OK, Dave?


00:39:12.000 --> 00:39:13.600
It's probably nothing, love.


00:39:13.700 --> 00:39:16.900
There is something wrong. I
should never have listened to you.


00:39:17.000 --> 00:39:18.765
You and your big ideas.


00:39:18.800 --> 00:39:23.000
Moving us into some old wreck
with damp and no central heating!


00:39:23.100 --> 00:39:24.800
I did it for you.
I did it for us.


00:39:24.900 --> 00:39:28.300
You did it for you. So you could
be the big man in the big house!


00:39:28.335 --> 00:39:29.800
What was I thinking?


00:39:29.900 --> 00:39:33.200
- What if we lose her?
- Don't say that.


00:39:33.300 --> 00:39:35.265
After trying for so long.


00:39:35.300 --> 00:39:39.700
All those tests and
doctors, the miscarriages.


00:39:41.200 --> 00:39:43.700
I thought she was our
piece of luck, our miracle.


00:39:43.800 --> 00:39:48.900
- Please, babe.
- We can't lose her. Not now.


00:39:49.000 --> 00:39:51.100
Come here, darling.


00:39:53.400 --> 00:39:55.200
It's OK.


00:40:19.900 --> 00:40:23.700
Don't you worry. Do you hear me?
Your dad will be back in a bit.


00:42:00.400 --> 00:42:02.400
The baby's back in hospital.


00:42:06.400 --> 00:42:09.300
Come on, I've got
something to show you.


00:42:31.200 --> 00:42:33.200
What is this place?


00:42:38.300 --> 00:42:42.400
I used to come here all the
time when I needed to think.


00:42:57.600 --> 00:43:01.500
If you wanna cry, that's OK.


00:43:01.535 --> 00:43:03.465
What?


00:43:03.500 --> 00:43:08.100
I used to cry all the
time... after my dad died.


00:43:10.300 --> 00:43:11.665
Sorry.


00:43:11.700 --> 00:43:13.700
I just wanted you to know.


00:43:29.600 --> 00:43:31.565
How do you do that?


00:43:31.600 --> 00:43:33.400
Put your hands
together like this.


00:43:36.400 --> 00:43:38.300
- Yeah.
- Now put your thumbs together.


00:43:38.400 --> 00:43:40.800
And now blow across
the top of your thumbs.


00:43:41.900 --> 00:43:42.900
Not so hard.


00:43:47.000 --> 00:43:49.200
See, you've just got to try.


00:44:38.100 --> 00:44:39.500
- Dad?
- Hmm?


00:44:40.600 --> 00:44:42.100
You know the baby?


00:44:42.200 --> 00:44:43.700
Not now, Mikey.


00:44:44.800 --> 00:44:47.100
I didn't realise you
wanted another one so much.


00:44:49.200 --> 00:44:50.800
What are you on about?


00:44:51.900 --> 00:44:54.100
You didn't tell me.


00:44:54.200 --> 00:44:56.400
Come on.


00:45:16.300 --> 00:45:17.400
Hey.


00:45:18.300 --> 00:45:21.400
Wake up. Wake up!


00:45:36.200 --> 00:45:38.600
You again?


00:45:38.700 --> 00:45:41.600
Of course it's me. You
scared me! You frightened me!


00:45:41.700 --> 00:45:44.600
I thought you'd given
up coming to pester me.


00:45:45.800 --> 00:45:48.000
I thought you'd
finally left me alone.


00:45:48.035 --> 00:45:49.800
Well, I'm here now.


00:45:51.000 --> 00:45:52.900
Well, you took your
bloody time, didn't you?


00:45:54.500 --> 00:45:58.300
My sister... She had
to go back to hospital.


00:45:59.600 --> 00:46:01.400
She's been really ill.


00:46:02.700 --> 00:46:04.565
Oh, well, there's a shock.


00:46:04.600 --> 00:46:08.800
Don't you care? The
doctors say she might...


00:46:08.835 --> 00:46:10.300
Die?


00:46:11.600 --> 00:46:12.965
Probably.


00:46:13.000 --> 00:46:15.300
It happens every day.


00:46:15.335 --> 00:46:17.100
Every minute.


00:46:17.200 --> 00:46:18.565
Every heartbeat.


00:46:18.600 --> 00:46:20.400
She's just a little baby.


00:46:23.100 --> 00:46:29.700
She's a speck... in
a boundless universe.


00:46:34.900 --> 00:46:36.500
I want to bring
someone to see you.


00:46:37.700 --> 00:46:39.900
What, someone to tell
you I'm really here?


00:46:39.935 --> 00:46:42.100
- Someone who'll know what to do.
- No.


00:46:42.135 --> 00:46:44.400
- They're clever.
- No.


00:46:44.500 --> 00:46:47.700
Well, what am I supposed
to do? Just tell me!


00:46:47.800 --> 00:46:50.100
My dad's sad, my
mum's sad, you're sad.


00:46:50.200 --> 00:46:52.600
I'm trying to help you. I
just wanna do something right!


00:46:52.700 --> 00:46:55.100
This bloody shed's about to
collapse and you won't move!


00:46:55.200 --> 00:46:59.400
You're nasty and spiteful
and I'm sick of you, but...


00:46:59.435 --> 00:47:01.200
But what?


00:47:04.200 --> 00:47:08.200
Bring the whole street.
Bring the whole damn town!


00:47:08.235 --> 00:47:11.000
Fine, I will.


00:48:00.500 --> 00:48:02.300
Are you ready for this? Yeah!


00:48:02.400 --> 00:48:04.300
It's dirty and dangerous.


00:48:04.400 --> 00:48:06.500
Really? Really.


00:48:09.200 --> 00:48:11.200
It's really cool, though.


00:48:33.500 --> 00:48:37.000
I brought my friend,
like I said. This is Mina.


00:48:37.035 --> 00:48:39.200
Girl.


00:48:40.700 --> 00:48:43.800
Sugar and spice and
all things nasty.


00:48:44.800 --> 00:48:46.550
Just ignore him.


00:48:46.585 --> 00:48:48.300
I got you this.


00:49:00.500 --> 00:49:03.665
Nectar.


00:49:03.700 --> 00:49:05.900
Drink of the dogs.


00:49:11.600 --> 00:49:13.400
Who are you?


00:49:13.500 --> 00:49:15.300
Mr Had Enough Of You.


00:49:15.335 --> 00:49:17.100
Don't be so rude.


00:49:18.100 --> 00:49:19.765
Oh, it's like that, is it?


00:49:19.800 --> 00:49:21.800
It is if you want
any more of this.


00:49:23.700 --> 00:49:25.600
You've got insects
in your hair.


00:49:32.100 --> 00:49:34.900
Yeah. They're delicious.


00:49:40.800 --> 00:49:42.800
You want one?


00:49:47.500 --> 00:49:50.600
- You feel like a dead person.
- I should be so lucky.


00:49:51.600 --> 00:49:55.600
It's calcification. The process
by which the body hardens,


00:49:55.700 --> 00:49:57.700
becomes inflexible.


00:49:57.735 --> 00:49:59.800
More beer.


00:50:01.000 --> 00:50:03.300
It's linked to
another process,


00:50:03.400 --> 00:50:06.100
by which the
mind, too, hardens,


00:50:06.135 --> 00:50:08.567
stops thinking and imagining.


00:50:08.602 --> 00:50:11.000
This process is ossification.


00:50:12.200 --> 00:50:15.400
- A bit of a show-off, your girlfriend,
in't she? - She's not my girlfriend.


00:50:15.500 --> 00:50:17.500
Oh, it's like that, is it?


00:50:32.600 --> 00:50:34.300
- Have you told anyone else?
- No one.


00:50:34.400 --> 00:50:37.600
- So, what do you think about him?
- Mm... I don't know!


00:50:37.635 --> 00:50:40.000
- But do you think he's like us?
- No.


00:50:40.100 --> 00:50:42.100
So, what is he, then?


00:50:55.200 --> 00:50:57.365
Dad?


00:50:57.400 --> 00:51:01.100
Your mum was right about that
damp. Never seen anything like this.


00:51:03.300 --> 00:51:05.300
Why didn't you tell me?


00:51:12.000 --> 00:51:15.200
That needs sorting.


00:51:15.300 --> 00:51:17.800
- I'll be in the shed if you need me.
- The shed?


00:51:52.300 --> 00:51:54.700
Sorry.


00:52:11.200 --> 00:52:14.900
Hello, cherub. What
are you doing back here?


00:52:15.800 --> 00:52:18.100
Is the baby not well?


00:52:19.200 --> 00:52:21.600
Oh, don't look so sad.


00:52:22.400 --> 00:52:25.400
Your sister's gonna
have a long life.


00:52:25.435 --> 00:52:28.100
She'll be old like me one day.


00:52:28.135 --> 00:52:30.100
You listen to Gracie.


00:52:31.800 --> 00:52:33.600
Oh, here.


00:52:35.500 --> 00:52:37.500
This is for you.


00:52:38.600 --> 00:52:41.600
And these are for your friend.


00:52:41.635 --> 00:52:44.565
- What are they?
- Cod-liver oil.


00:52:44.600 --> 00:52:47.900
- For your friend with Arthur.
- You remembered!


00:52:48.000 --> 00:52:51.300
And tell him from me
to keep on dancing.


00:52:51.400 --> 00:52:53.565
Thanks, Grace.


00:52:53.600 --> 00:52:55.700
Did you have a nice
visit with your son?


00:52:56.600 --> 00:52:59.900
He hopes... in
a couple of weeks.


00:53:00.800 --> 00:53:05.100
I could come and see you. For a
proper visit, in the ward upstairs.


00:53:06.000 --> 00:53:08.300
That'd be grand.


00:53:08.400 --> 00:53:11.965
Oh! But say that
you get too busy,


00:53:12.000 --> 00:53:16.400
or... or I'm out dancing,
maybe, and we miss each other,


00:53:16.435 --> 00:53:20.200
just remember, them as
can walk should walk.


00:53:20.300 --> 00:53:23.000
Them as can dance
should dance.


00:53:23.900 --> 00:53:26.900
And them as can fly...


00:53:27.000 --> 00:53:29.000
Well, you know the
rest, don't you?


00:53:48.500 --> 00:53:51.500
It's not because she
came early or anything.


00:53:51.600 --> 00:53:53.500
It's her heart.


00:53:54.700 --> 00:53:57.100
It's not working properly.


00:54:00.200 --> 00:54:02.500
The doctors are
working really hard.


00:54:25.000 --> 00:54:27.300
I'm sorry, baby.


00:54:29.900 --> 00:54:31.900
Get strong.


00:54:32.900 --> 00:54:34.900
Please get strong.


00:55:24.900 --> 00:55:26.900
I could have swore
I put more in there.


00:55:38.600 --> 00:55:41.100
You were right,
Mikey. This is a dump.


00:55:42.000 --> 00:55:45.200
I should never have brought
you all to a place like this.


00:56:10.200 --> 00:56:12.200
Dad, what are you doing?


00:56:12.300 --> 00:56:15.200
I told your mother it was coming
down, so by God, it's gonna come down.


00:56:15.235 --> 00:56:16.500
Get out the way.


00:56:17.300 --> 00:56:19.465
Dad! Please, not now!


00:56:19.500 --> 00:56:22.300
Piss off, Mikey! Let a man
do one thing right, at least.


00:56:22.335 --> 00:56:24.500
Dad! You can't!


00:56:26.900 --> 00:56:29.000
Get back in the
house. Shift it.


00:56:30.400 --> 00:56:31.900
What you gonna do?


00:56:32.000 --> 00:56:34.100
Don't we even have sodding
matches in this house?


00:56:34.200 --> 00:56:36.500
- Dad! You're not going to...
- You, bed.


00:56:36.600 --> 00:56:38.300
- Dad.
- Move it.


00:56:52.600 --> 00:56:56.000
Come on! He's
gonna burn it down!


00:56:56.100 --> 00:56:58.300
- Ah, let it burn.
- Move it!


00:57:03.200 --> 00:57:06.100
Ah, get off me.


00:58:18.800 --> 00:58:21.000
Stay here. I'll
come back later.


00:58:29.300 --> 00:58:31.300
Dad.


00:58:37.000 --> 00:58:38.900
My little baby.


00:58:40.600 --> 00:58:42.600
Little girl, Michael.


00:58:44.700 --> 00:58:46.700
What can I do?


00:58:49.300 --> 00:58:51.300
What can I do?


00:58:52.400 --> 00:58:55.900
Come on. Come on.


00:59:35.700 --> 00:59:37.800
- My dad burned down the shed.
- What?


00:59:37.835 --> 00:59:39.900
- I burned my hand.
- What about him?


00:59:40.000 --> 00:59:42.500
- I left him in the woods.
- Come inside, but be quiet.


00:59:42.600 --> 00:59:46.200
- We have to take him somewhere safe.
- Don't wake my mum.


00:59:57.800 --> 01:00:02.000
Ashes to ashes.
Ashes and dust.


01:00:11.900 --> 01:00:13.900
Nearly there.


01:00:23.800 --> 01:00:26.265
Oh, I'm tired.


01:00:26.300 --> 01:00:28.500
So unbelievably tired.


01:00:37.100 --> 01:00:39.000
Who are you?


01:00:40.800 --> 01:00:43.300
I'm ancient as the earth.


01:00:46.900 --> 01:00:49.200
Have you got a name?


01:00:49.235 --> 01:00:51.500
My name is Skellig.


01:01:04.900 --> 01:01:09.200
Dad. It's really late.
You've been working all day.


01:01:09.300 --> 01:01:13.100
Be careful in your room. The
floor's done, but it needs more work.


01:01:16.800 --> 01:01:19.200
It's going to be
really nice in here.


01:02:05.600 --> 01:02:08.400
- All for you.
- Let me help you.


01:02:10.300 --> 01:02:12.800
No. No, don't touch me.


01:02:15.500 --> 01:02:18.200
I'll make you
more comfortable.


01:02:19.100 --> 01:02:20.200
- Trust me.
- Get off me.


01:02:20.300 --> 01:02:22.300
Come on. Come on!


01:02:22.400 --> 01:02:23.700
No, don't.


01:02:37.100 --> 01:02:40.000
Wow. Michael, I'm scared.


01:02:55.300 --> 01:02:57.300
What is this?


01:02:58.200 --> 01:03:00.500
They're amazing!


01:03:00.535 --> 01:03:02.800
They're no good.


01:03:19.700 --> 01:03:21.700
Let me sleep.


01:03:26.000 --> 01:03:27.800
OK.


01:03:48.900 --> 01:03:51.600
There are so many wings here.


01:03:51.700 --> 01:03:54.565
Insects, bats, birds.


01:03:54.600 --> 01:03:57.200
- Angels, even.
- None look like his, though.


01:03:58.200 --> 01:04:02.500
- What is he, Mina?
- It's like he's something... in between.


01:04:05.900 --> 01:04:08.400
I don't see how these
angels actually fly.


01:04:08.435 --> 01:04:10.200
They just float.


01:04:10.235 --> 01:04:12.100
Mina...


01:04:12.200 --> 01:04:14.800
- Do you think Skellig could ever fly?
- Be quiet.


01:04:14.900 --> 01:04:21.700
What about this? It says here that
dinosaurs descended into birds.


01:04:21.800 --> 01:04:23.800
Maybe we'll change too.


01:04:24.900 --> 01:04:27.700
This isn't how we're
supposed to be forever.


01:04:27.735 --> 01:04:31.900
Maybe we're always
changing. Evolving.


01:04:32.000 --> 01:04:34.300
Like it never stops.


01:04:35.000 --> 01:04:37.300
Michael, we are extraordinary.


01:04:42.800 --> 01:04:45.900
"Michael! We're
extraordinary, Michael!"


01:04:46.000 --> 01:04:48.000
Shut up.


01:04:48.100 --> 01:04:50.600
"Maybe we'll change too. "


01:04:50.700 --> 01:04:53.700
- Thinking about the girlfriend?
- She's not my girlfriend.


01:04:53.735 --> 01:04:55.465
Yeah, right. So,
spill it, then.


01:04:55.500 --> 01:04:58.000
Let's hear the details.
What's your girlfriend's name?


01:04:58.100 --> 01:05:00.065
Where's she go to school?


01:05:00.100 --> 01:05:02.400
Mina doesn't go to
school. Her mum tutors her.


01:05:02.500 --> 01:05:05.100
You what? Is she
thick or something?


01:05:08.500 --> 01:05:10.400
"Michael, don't go!"


01:05:10.435 --> 01:05:12.300
"We're extraordinary!"


01:05:12.335 --> 01:05:14.700
Where's he going?


01:05:54.800 --> 01:05:56.800
I thought you
weren't going to come.


01:05:59.100 --> 01:06:01.500
Where is he?


01:06:03.600 --> 01:06:05.100
Listen. What's that?


01:06:17.700 --> 01:06:19.100
They're feeding him.


01:06:23.800 --> 01:06:26.400
Careful. He's changed.


01:06:26.435 --> 01:06:29.000
He's much stronger.


01:06:47.200 --> 01:06:49.200
Come here.


01:08:17.200 --> 01:08:19.200
Remember this night.


01:08:26.600 --> 01:08:29.200
Did it really happen?


01:08:29.235 --> 01:08:30.200
It did.


01:08:33.900 --> 01:08:36.800
My hand... it's better.


01:08:36.835 --> 01:08:38.800
What?


01:08:41.000 --> 01:08:43.500
I think he healed me, Mina.


01:09:12.500 --> 01:09:14.100
What's going on, Mikey?


01:09:14.800 --> 01:09:18.500
You don't have to worry, Dad. Not
any more. Everything's gonna be OK.


01:09:18.535 --> 01:09:20.300
Look, Michael...


01:09:21.300 --> 01:09:23.300
I've got to tell
you something.


01:09:25.200 --> 01:09:28.400
Alcohol... is
never the answer.


01:09:30.200 --> 01:09:32.200
Hey. I'm being serious here.


01:09:33.000 --> 01:09:36.500
- OK, I'm not one to talk...
- Dad, what are you on about?


01:09:37.500 --> 01:09:40.300
Look, what were you doing up
in the middle of the night?


01:09:40.335 --> 01:09:43.800
Huh? And those missing beers?


01:09:44.800 --> 01:09:46.900
Don't be stupid. I
haven't taken your beers.


01:09:46.935 --> 01:09:48.965
Well, they've
been disappearing.


01:09:49.000 --> 01:09:52.300
- It wasn't me, I swear it.
- Well, who is it, then, Michael?


01:09:53.900 --> 01:09:56.200
The bloody Sugar Plum Fairy?


01:10:00.700 --> 01:10:03.200
Are you sure you've
got everything?


01:10:04.400 --> 01:10:07.600
- I think so.
- We've got to make him strong again, Mina.


01:10:07.635 --> 01:10:09.600
Strong enough to fly.


01:10:13.700 --> 01:10:17.800
Grapes. Only good for
one thing, they are.


01:10:18.700 --> 01:10:21.500
- He means wine.
- I don't like 'em either.


01:10:22.200 --> 01:10:25.800
Now, you should take these, once a day,
and I'll get you more when they run out.


01:10:25.900 --> 01:10:28.500
- What is it?
- Cod-liver oil.


01:10:28.600 --> 01:10:31.300
- For your joints.
- Cod.


01:10:31.400 --> 01:10:33.500
I don't like fish.


01:10:33.600 --> 01:10:37.000
They're stinking, slithering,
slimy, scaly things, they are.


01:10:37.035 --> 01:10:39.300
Talking of stinking...


01:10:45.400 --> 01:10:48.600
- What now?
- It's all the spiders and insects you eat.


01:10:49.600 --> 01:10:52.400
- I don't need that.
- Yeah, you do.


01:10:53.100 --> 01:10:55.200
What you really need is
a proper dental regime.


01:10:55.300 --> 01:10:58.200
Brushing, flossing...
occasional trip to the dentist.


01:10:58.300 --> 01:11:00.000
I'd take it if I were you.


01:11:01.500 --> 01:11:03.500
You've got to open it for him.


01:11:21.800 --> 01:11:23.765
It's not bad, that.


01:11:23.800 --> 01:11:25.500
You're not meant
to swallow it.


01:11:26.300 --> 01:11:28.050
What you supposed
to do with it, then?


01:11:28.085 --> 01:11:29.800
- You're supposed to spit it out.
- Why?


01:11:39.400 --> 01:11:40.900
What's the point?


01:11:52.700 --> 01:11:54.600
What if someone comes?


01:11:54.635 --> 01:11:56.700
Stop worrying.


01:11:57.800 --> 01:11:59.700
Is there no end
to your torture?


01:12:00.700 --> 01:12:02.700
It's for your feathers.


01:12:04.000 --> 01:12:07.600
It'll make them
silky and smooth,


01:12:08.700 --> 01:12:11.600
and... and add volume!


01:12:38.200 --> 01:12:41.065
I hate water.
Home of the fishes.


01:12:41.100 --> 01:12:43.900
- Stinky, slimy, scaly...
- Yeah, we know.


01:12:52.600 --> 01:12:54.565
It's getting cold.


01:12:54.600 --> 01:12:57.600
- We should go in.
- Always on the move, in't ya?


01:12:59.500 --> 01:13:02.900
Leave the shed, go to the tower,
leave the tower, go back to the tower.


01:13:03.000 --> 01:13:06.000
Come on. Before
you catch a cold.


01:13:18.200 --> 01:13:19.800
Did you do that?


01:13:23.600 --> 01:13:25.500
What?


01:13:30.700 --> 01:13:34.400
Then Daedalus and Icarus
stand on the edge of the cliff.


01:13:34.500 --> 01:13:38.100
The sun's beating down. They're not
sure whether the wings'll work or not.


01:13:39.100 --> 01:13:43.400
But they're ready to jump.
Then there's a big gust of wind.


01:13:45.000 --> 01:13:47.000
Wind. Get it?


01:13:48.600 --> 01:13:52.300
Since Mr Coot here
finds it all so amusing,


01:13:52.400 --> 01:13:56.500
maybe you could inform him, Michael,
of what happens to our feathered men?


01:13:56.535 --> 01:14:00.600
They do fly, but Icarus...
he gets too close to the sun.


01:14:00.700 --> 01:14:04.300
Their wings melt and they
crash into the sea and die.


01:14:04.900 --> 01:14:06.365
Thank you, Michael.


01:14:06.400 --> 01:14:09.900
Right. We've all heard a little of
what Michael's been reading at home.


01:14:10.000 --> 01:14:12.900
So, who's going to tell him what
we've all been learning here?


01:14:12.935 --> 01:14:15.000
Mikey, don't forget.


01:14:15.900 --> 01:14:17.900
Leakey?


01:14:19.300 --> 01:14:21.000
Uh, our insides?


01:14:21.100 --> 01:14:23.300
Come in.


01:14:23.900 --> 01:14:26.665
OK.


01:14:26.700 --> 01:14:28.100
Michael?


01:14:28.200 --> 01:14:30.200
You've got a
message from home.


01:14:35.700 --> 01:14:38.200
- You've got to try to help my sister!
- Oh...


01:14:40.000 --> 01:14:42.100
Please!


01:14:42.200 --> 01:14:44.465
She has...


01:14:44.500 --> 01:14:47.400
She's really ill. She
has to have an operation.


01:14:47.500 --> 01:14:49.450
She... Her heart's really...


01:14:49.485 --> 01:14:51.400
She might... She might not...


01:14:51.435 --> 01:14:53.500
I can't help her.


01:14:53.600 --> 01:14:55.600
I can't help anyone.


01:14:56.500 --> 01:14:59.400
But my hand healed! You
can save her, I know...


01:14:59.435 --> 01:15:02.165
No. No more of that.


01:15:02.200 --> 01:15:06.200
I've had an eternity of that, and I
want it to stop. You understand me?


01:15:06.300 --> 01:15:09.300
That can't just be it!
You can't just give up!


01:15:09.400 --> 01:15:11.900
I told you, at the first.


01:15:14.300 --> 01:15:16.300
Leave me alone.


01:15:20.100 --> 01:15:22.700
Why are you so...
so unhopeful?


01:15:37.600 --> 01:15:39.500
I'm sorry, Michael.


01:15:41.800 --> 01:15:43.800
I'm so sorry.


01:16:15.400 --> 01:16:18.200
Michael! What's happened?


01:16:22.800 --> 01:16:24.800
Are you OK?


01:16:31.300 --> 01:16:33.300
It's not the baby, is it?


01:16:34.300 --> 01:16:37.965
- It's over.
- What do you mean?


01:16:38.000 --> 01:16:41.000
She's gonna die and there's
nothing I can do about it.


01:16:52.100 --> 01:16:54.100
Sleep well, both of you.


01:17:01.000 --> 01:17:03.200
Never had a friend
sleep over before.


01:17:04.300 --> 01:17:06.300
Bet you've had loads.


01:17:07.900 --> 01:17:09.900
Yeah.


01:17:11.000 --> 01:17:14.000
- But not...
- But not what?


01:17:15.800 --> 01:17:18.100
- Not a girl.
- Oh.


01:17:24.100 --> 01:17:26.100
I'd have liked a
brother or sister.


01:17:30.100 --> 01:17:32.600
I didn't really
want... the baby.


01:17:34.900 --> 01:17:36.900
I just liked it
the three of us.


01:17:37.800 --> 01:17:40.700
I didn't want to move
house, so I didn't help.


01:17:42.100 --> 01:17:44.365
Then she came early.


01:17:44.400 --> 01:17:47.500
- It's not your fault, Michael.
- How do you know?


01:17:48.500 --> 01:17:50.965
I know because...


01:17:51.000 --> 01:17:54.200
I used to think that...
if I'd been good...


01:17:55.100 --> 01:17:57.350
if I'd never been bad...


01:17:57.385 --> 01:17:59.600
then my dad wouldn't have...


01:17:59.700 --> 01:18:03.200
Anyway, it's not true.
Not for me, not for you.


01:18:07.800 --> 01:18:09.800
What happened to him?


01:18:10.600 --> 01:18:12.900
He was just...


01:18:13.000 --> 01:18:15.450
He didn't want
to live any more.


01:18:15.485 --> 01:18:17.900
He was just tired of living.


01:18:19.100 --> 01:18:21.100
He was just tired out.


01:18:23.200 --> 01:18:25.100
You must really miss him.


01:18:26.000 --> 01:18:29.300
Yes, I do. Even the sad him.


01:18:31.900 --> 01:18:34.500
Do you think your mum
will get married again?


01:18:34.600 --> 01:18:38.500
Then perhaps... you'll have
a brother or sister after all.


01:18:38.600 --> 01:18:40.400
It'll never happen.


01:18:41.200 --> 01:18:43.600
My mum says she's like a swan.


01:18:45.500 --> 01:18:47.600
Why a swan?


01:18:48.800 --> 01:18:50.800
It's just...


01:18:50.900 --> 01:18:53.100
swans mate for life.


01:19:01.300 --> 01:19:04.500
They've got a heart surgeon
coming up from London.


01:19:04.600 --> 01:19:06.865
He'll do the
operation this evening.


01:19:06.900 --> 01:19:09.365
Mina's mum said you could
stay at theirs again tonight.


01:19:09.400 --> 01:19:12.200
I don't want to stay there! I want
to come to the hospital with you.


01:19:12.235 --> 01:19:14.600
Me and your mum think it would
be better if you went to school.


01:19:14.635 --> 01:19:16.900
Well, you're wrong! You're
just leaving me out again.


01:19:17.000 --> 01:19:20.365
Mikey, trust me. It'll
just be upsetting for you.


01:19:20.400 --> 01:19:23.700
And also, today, there's nothing you
can do. You'll just be hanging around.


01:19:23.735 --> 01:19:26.900
- I want to come with you!
- No. Sorry.


01:19:27.000 --> 01:19:28.700
- We know best.
- Do you?


01:19:29.700 --> 01:19:31.700
What's that supposed to mean?


01:19:33.800 --> 01:19:37.600
- Right. It's settled, then.
- I'm not going to school, not today.


01:19:37.700 --> 01:19:39.500
- You will do as you're told.
- Why should I?


01:19:39.600 --> 01:19:41.700
You think you know best,
but you don't know anything.


01:19:41.800 --> 01:19:44.400
You just care about the house. All
you do is work on the bloody thing.


01:19:44.500 --> 01:19:46.700
- Don't say bloody.
- Bloody, bloody, bloody...


01:19:46.800 --> 01:19:48.700
Right, that is enough!


01:19:48.800 --> 01:19:52.500
You're going to school today if I
have to drag you there my bloody self!


01:19:52.600 --> 01:19:55.150
- You don't know anything about me.
- You little shit.


01:19:55.185 --> 01:19:57.700
- You just want me out of the way.
- OK, that is enough.


01:19:57.800 --> 01:20:00.165
You don't include me,
you hardly talk to me,


01:20:00.200 --> 01:20:03.400
you never told me you wanted a baby,
and now you're not telling me the truth!


01:20:03.435 --> 01:20:05.900
I know she might
die. I know it.


01:20:11.300 --> 01:20:14.200
I love you. OK?


01:20:15.900 --> 01:20:17.900
I love you.


01:20:20.000 --> 01:20:22.000
Come on.


01:20:55.600 --> 01:20:57.600
Back in a sec.


01:21:12.400 --> 01:21:15.500
- You looking for someone, love?
- Grace.


01:21:16.600 --> 01:21:20.700
I'm very sorry. Gracie
passed away late last night.


01:21:20.800 --> 01:21:23.400
- Passed away?
- I'm sorry.


01:21:25.200 --> 01:21:28.500
I was coming to
see her. I promised.


01:21:29.400 --> 01:21:30.900
She's gone, love.


01:21:43.300 --> 01:21:48.300
You just remember, them
as can dance should dance.


01:21:48.400 --> 01:21:50.665
And them as can fly...


01:21:50.700 --> 01:21:52.700
You know the rest, don't you?


01:21:56.600 --> 01:21:57.600
Mum!


01:21:59.500 --> 01:22:01.900
- Where have you been? I was looking...
- I've got to go.


01:22:02.000 --> 01:22:04.100
Wait. I wanted to
talk to you, darling.


01:22:04.200 --> 01:22:06.600
I want you to know that,
no matter what happens...


01:22:06.635 --> 01:22:08.700
Mum... we'll
always have each other.


01:22:08.800 --> 01:22:11.800
- I want you to remember that.
- I'm OK, Mum, honest.


01:22:11.900 --> 01:22:14.300
- Where are you going?
- Can't give up, Mum. Mustn't ever give up.


01:22:14.335 --> 01:22:16.300
- Gotta fly!
- Michael!


01:22:44.600 --> 01:22:46.900
Mikey?


01:23:13.000 --> 01:23:17.100
Where were you? Don't you even want
to ask how I did in the competition?


01:23:17.135 --> 01:23:18.765
Leakey, I'm really sorry.


01:23:18.800 --> 01:23:20.900
Is this where you come to get
all loved up with your girlfriend?


01:23:21.000 --> 01:23:22.700
- No!
- Well, what is this place?


01:23:22.800 --> 01:23:25.200
Leakey, I want to explain.


01:23:26.400 --> 01:23:28.900
What are you hiding
from me? Move!


01:23:28.935 --> 01:23:30.600
No, Leakey! Stop!


01:23:34.900 --> 01:23:36.500
Get off me!


01:23:41.300 --> 01:23:42.700
Come back!


01:23:43.400 --> 01:23:44.600
Skellig! Get up!


01:23:44.700 --> 01:23:46.800
Skellig!


01:23:50.200 --> 01:23:53.600
Get out! Go! You'll
ruin everything!


01:23:54.800 --> 01:23:57.000
What's this?


01:23:57.100 --> 01:23:58.965
Tell me!


01:23:59.000 --> 01:24:01.000
Nothing, just go!


01:24:01.700 --> 01:24:03.800
Go!


01:24:08.600 --> 01:24:10.500
I thought we was best mates.


01:24:51.300 --> 01:24:53.300
Come here.


01:24:56.100 --> 01:24:58.100
You're hurt, Michael.


01:25:01.900 --> 01:25:05.100
You can fly, Skellig.
You can fly to her.


01:25:05.900 --> 01:25:08.400
I know you can.


01:25:11.600 --> 01:25:13.500
What are you doing?


01:25:14.700 --> 01:25:17.600
I believe in you.
Even if you don't.


01:26:47.700 --> 01:26:49.700
Sleep, Michael.


01:27:02.200 --> 01:27:04.800
I don't think she'll
make it through the night.


01:30:30.600 --> 01:30:32.600
Michael.


01:30:33.400 --> 01:30:36.300
Michael, wake up. Michael?


01:30:36.400 --> 01:30:38.300
- Oh!
- Mina!


01:30:42.900 --> 01:30:44.900
How did you get here?


01:31:01.000 --> 01:31:03.465
She's so strong.


01:31:03.500 --> 01:31:07.500
She's amazed all the
doctors, that's for sure.


01:31:07.535 --> 01:31:09.800
Haven't you, little one?


01:31:09.835 --> 01:31:12.400
It's so strange.


01:31:12.500 --> 01:31:17.800
I had a dream this man was
watching over us while we slept.


01:31:17.900 --> 01:31:21.100
He was filthy. Tattered shirt.


01:31:22.000 --> 01:31:24.200
And I could swear
there were... wings.


01:31:25.600 --> 01:31:28.100
Or feathers, at least.


01:31:28.135 --> 01:31:29.665
Sounds horrible.


01:31:29.700 --> 01:31:32.700
No. I wasn't scared at all.


01:31:33.600 --> 01:31:36.000
It was like I knew
he was there to help.


01:31:36.035 --> 01:31:38.400
- The way he looked at me.
- Blimey.


01:31:38.500 --> 01:31:41.000
Some dream.


01:31:42.900 --> 01:31:45.000
Don't you think it's
time she had a name?


01:31:45.100 --> 01:31:48.900
Yeah. It's just, nothing
seems quite right.


01:31:49.600 --> 01:31:51.500
Not for this little one.


01:31:51.600 --> 01:31:54.700
Grace. How about Grace?


01:31:58.900 --> 01:32:00.900
It could be.


01:32:03.400 --> 01:32:05.300
Hello, Grace.


01:32:06.700 --> 01:32:09.100
Hello, Grace.


01:32:13.600 --> 01:32:16.165
Oh, there you are.


01:32:16.200 --> 01:32:20.100
- # Why don't you get back into bed? #
- This! This is what you call a song.


01:32:20.135 --> 01:32:23.600
# Why don't you get back into bed?
Why don't you get back into bed?


01:32:23.635 --> 01:32:25.900
# Why don't you
get back into bed? #


01:32:26.000 --> 01:32:29.800
# Reasons to be cheerful, part three #
Reasons to be cheerful, one, two, three!


01:32:29.900 --> 01:32:33.965
# Summer, Buddy Holly, the working
folly, Good Golly Miss Molly and boats


01:32:34.000 --> 01:32:38.500
# Hammersmith Palais, the Bolshoi Ballet,
jump back in the alley and nanny goats #


01:32:38.535 --> 01:32:41.300
Is that a smile? Is
that a smile I see?


01:32:41.400 --> 01:32:43.100
- Yes! There it is!
- Get off!


01:33:05.300 --> 01:33:07.800
- That was brilliant.
- Thanks, man.


01:33:11.200 --> 01:33:13.100
- All good.
- All right.


01:33:18.600 --> 01:33:20.600
- See you later.
- See you at school.


01:33:28.400 --> 01:33:31.600
Look what your
daddy's made for you!


01:33:43.000 --> 01:33:44.500
She's home.


01:33:54.100 --> 01:33:56.200
I should never
have blamed you.


01:33:56.300 --> 01:33:58.900
Hey, don't be silly.


01:33:59.000 --> 01:34:02.500
- We're swans, you and me.
- What?


01:34:02.600 --> 01:34:05.300
Nothing, it's just
something our son told me.


01:34:23.100 --> 01:34:25.100
All for you.


01:34:31.100 --> 01:34:33.100
27 and 53.


01:34:33.200 --> 01:34:37.100
Sweetest of nectars.
Food of the dogs.


01:34:44.400 --> 01:34:46.765
You're a pair of
angels, you are.


01:34:46.800 --> 01:34:49.900
- You saved my sister.
- A heart of fire, that one.


01:34:51.200 --> 01:34:53.300
Gave me strength.
Just like her brother.


01:34:59.800 --> 01:35:01.200
Is this goodbye?


01:35:02.800 --> 01:35:04.300
Where will you go?


01:35:05.600 --> 01:35:06.700
Somewhere.


01:35:14.000 --> 01:35:18.900
- What are you?
- I'm something... like you.


01:35:19.600 --> 01:35:21.500
Something like a bird.


01:35:21.600 --> 01:35:23.900
- Something like an angel?
- Yeah.


01:35:27.600 --> 01:35:29.700
Something like that.


01:35:41.500 --> 01:35:44.300
It's weird how things can be
so normal so quickly again.


01:35:44.400 --> 01:35:46.800
- Nice normal?
- Yeah.


01:35:51.000 --> 01:35:53.800
Are you gonna tell
your sister one day?


01:35:53.835 --> 01:35:55.500
Do you think
she'll believe you?


01:35:55.535 --> 01:35:57.500
If we both tell her.


01:35:59.000 --> 01:36:01.000
Come on.


01:36:02.200 --> 01:36:05.700
- Got a project to hand in tomorrow.
- What is it on this time?


01:36:05.735 --> 01:36:08.000
Science. Darwin.


01:36:08.100 --> 01:36:10.000
Don't suppose you
want to do it for me?


01:36:10.100 --> 01:36:13.365
Erm... Maybe. It'll
cost you, though.


01:36:13.400 --> 01:36:17.100
You've changed, you know that?
Where's the Mina I used to know?


01:36:17.135 --> 01:36:18.865
She's evolved.


01:36:18.900 --> 01:36:21.600
Yeah, well, you're still
rubbish at footy, though.

